{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_prevote_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json,copy\nold=json.load(open('submission-vote-check.json'));p=json.load(open('vote-check-plan.json'))\ncid='C_real_vote_type';bid='BIND_real_vote_consumer';q=copy.deepcopy(old['candidate']['question'])\nq.update(audit_spec_version=6,question='Can a delayed genuine pre-vote grant carrying the same numeric term as a newly entered real campaign count toward leadership before a majority of real vote grants arrives?',importance='Mixing pre-vote and real-vote support would allow authority acquisition from replies that do not record an actual vote. The checked consequence is local real-campaign eligibility, not a conflicting-leader or client witness.',contexts=['Three fixed bootstrapped voters; AsyncStorageWrites and PreVote enabled','A genuine pre-vote majority starts real candidacy while the third pre-vote grant remains held','The retained pre-vote response and real vote responses share the same numeric term'],event_paths=['Campaign -> pre-candidate and three actual pre-vote grants after local storage work','Release self and peer-2 pre-vote grants -> real campaign at next term and genuine real grants held','Release peer-3 pre-vote grant, then real self/peer grants; measure leader role and real-grant ledger'],counterevidence=['stepCandidate selects MsgVoteResp during real candidacy, ignoring MsgPreVoteResp even when its term matches.','becomeCandidate resets the previously accepted pre-vote map before entering the new real term.'],unknowns=[],trigger_rationale='The prior check established only lower-term filtering. Here the original pre-vote term equals the actual real term, so response type and campaign reset must supply the distinction. The producer follows a real pre-vote majority; no synthetic response is introduced.')\nclaim=copy.deepcopy(old['candidate']['obligation']);claim['id']=cid\nclaim['description']='A real candidate must not acquire leadership using pre-vote grants, even when their numeric term matches; a majority of delivered real vote grants for that campaign is necessary.'\nclaim['scope']=dict(description='One actual pre-vote campaign advances through a pre-vote majority into real candidacy; a third pre-vote grant with matching numeric term is delivered before real self and peer grants.',assumptions=['Three fixed voters, PreVote enabled and AsyncStorageWrites; sequential RawNode calls and FIFO local work.','No timers, competing candidates, configuration changes, snapshots or restart in the measured suffix.','MemoryStorage models no-crash storage completion; real grant capture verifies actual stored term/vote.'],excluded=['General consensus correctness, physical crash safety or client consequences.','General pre-vote liveness, clock/lease assumptions and arbitrary candidate interactions.'])\nclaim['grounding'].update(binding_ids=[bid],derivation='The candidate consumer comment expressly requires responses corresponding to its candidacy and notes stale pre-vote replies can occur in the same term during real candidacy. Step grants pre-votes without recording a real vote; their response term comes from the request. Majority VoteResult defines winning support. These sources yield the local duty that a real campaign requires real grants, not same-term pre-vote grants.',applicability='Fixed three-voter real campaign entered through the implementation pre-vote path.',alternatives=['Pre-vote majority authorizes starting a real campaign, not immediate leadership.','A same-term pre-vote response need not be excluded by the numeric term gate; the response-type gate is the relevant protection.'])\nb=copy.deepcopy(old['candidate']['bindings'][0]);b['id']=bid;b['description']='stepCandidate selects the response type corresponding to pre-candidate versus real candidate before polling grants.';b['associations']=[dict(claim_id=cid,source_ids=['S_candidate_follower','S_step','S_campaign','S_roles','S_majority'],rationale='Real campaign majority cannot include a pre-vote reply that merely shares its term.')]\np.update(claim_id=cid,binding_ids=[bid],description='Retain the third genuine pre-vote reply while self and peer 2 start the real campaign; deliver it at the same numeric term, then release genuine real votes under four fixed phases.')\nh=p['harness'];h['description']='TestAssuranceDelayedPreVoteGrant; actual bootstrap, pre-campaign, pre-vote majority, real campaign and four response releases.'\nh['semantic_changes']=['MemoryStorage models crash-free storage completion.','Deterministic transport holds actual pre-vote and real-vote grants after FIFO local storage completion.','The independent ledger counts only delivered MsgVoteResp from distinct fixed voters at the real campaign term; public BasicStatus supplies leadership.']\nl=h['legality'];l.update(binding_ids=[bid],derivation='Bootstrap and apply configuration on three empty RawNodes with PreVote enabled. One Campaign produces three actual MsgPreVoteResp messages at next term; hold them after local workers finish. No persistence of a real vote is assumed for pre-votes. Release self and peer-2 pre-vote replies; the implementation resets vote support and starts the actual real campaign. Capture its three real grants, checking each producer stored term and Vote=1. The retained peer-3 pre-vote and new real grants have equal terms. Release that pre-vote, real self, real peer 2 and real peer 3, draining fixed permitted work after each. No second Campaign call or synthetic vote is used. Responses and their types/terms are unmodified.',applicability='Single goroutine, reliable FIFO local workers, no external timer or term input. All grant holds occur in transport after attached responses were released by completed local storage work.',alternatives=['Pre-vote grant capture reads stored HardState diagnostically but does not require a recorded vote, since pre-vote does not persist one.','A real grant still requires its actual producer vote in storage at capture.'])\nmon=p['monitors'][0];mon.update(id='M_real_vote_type',checker_id='real_vote_type',binding_ids=[bid]);mon['grounding'].update(binding_ids=[bid],derivation='Independent ledger admits only original delivered MsgVoteResp with the real campaign term. Original MsgPreVoteResp is delivered but never added even with matching term. Compare observed leadership from BasicStatus against two distinct real-grant senders. The implementation vote map is never read. Prerequisite and result identities remain request/phase/node/campaign_term; every fixed phase completes regardless of the predicate.',applicability='Four release operations after actual pre-vote majority and real-candidate admission; no outcome-dependent filtering.',alternatives=['A pending candidate after delayed pre-vote or one real grant is permitted.','Real self plus peer 2 provides a permitted current-real-majority control.'])\nprop=p['observable_properties'][0];prop.update(checker_id='real_vote_type',description='Leadership at each fixed checkpoint requires at least two genuine delivered real vote grants; matching-term pre-vote grants do not contribute.')\np['uncertainties']=['One fixed pre-vote-to-real transition and four checkpoints, not general pre-vote safety or liveness.','No crash, competing leader or client consequence is observed.']\njson.dump(p,open('prevote-check-plan.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='check',rationale='Check the separate same-term response-type boundary using the accepted campaign-support map and a real pre-vote producer history.',candidate=dict(action='obligation',question=q,rationale='Create an independent local response-type eligibility obligation; the prior lower-term result does not cover this equal-term case.',obligation=claim,bindings=[b]),plan_path='prevote-check-plan.json',harness_path='delayed_prevote_test.go',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S_candidate_follower','S_step','S_roles','S_campaign','S_majority'],answered='The consumer explicitly distinguishes pre-vote and real-vote response types because stale pre-vote replies can arrive in the real term. Pre-vote response terms are copied from future-term requests without recording a real vote. The new fixed driver traverses that actual producer path and counts only delivered real grants independently.',remaining=['Fresh execution and review must establish the same-term pre-vote input and all four completed comparisons.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='This isolates a guard not exercised by delayed lower-term replies and uses the already mapped campaign support lifecycle.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-prevote-check.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_prevote_check.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_19-39-39-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-prevote-check.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
